WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.820
Apple just dropped a hint that ChatGPT and Claude could soon live inside your smart home display. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 222. There is a weekend video feed built with Claude, ChatGPT picking wine at the supermarket, a deep dive on how ChatBots guess the next word and quick bits. Apple is preparing a new 7-inch home view smart home display, Analytics Insight Reports. It is meant to support outside ChatBots on top of Apple's own voice assistant Siri.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.500
A chatbot is a kind of artificial intelligence or AI.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:37.240
That means software you talk to in ordinary words, the way you text a person.

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:41.440
Siri is the talking helper already built into Apple phones and speakers.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:46.380
Picture home view as a small talking tablet that lives on the kitchen counter instead of

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:46.960
in your pocket.

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.040
Seven inches is about the size of a paperbacked book held in your hands.

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:57.420
Early test software for the upcoming iOS 27.3 update contains a brand new section labeled

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:03.580
conversational apps. iOS is the software that runs iPhones. This test copy looks built

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:08.900
so the screen can show and run chat services from companies such as OpenAI and Anthropic.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:14.440
OpenAI makes chat GPT, the chatbot many people already type questions into,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:20.660
Anthropic makes Claude, another chatbot that replies in everyday language. Conversational apps

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:25.720
is like being allowed extra chat apps on a phone instead of only the built-in messages app.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:31.720
The same test code also lists two-way audio routing, conversation session management, and

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:35.100
the ability to handle interruptions so voice chats can feel natural.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.500
Two-way audio is like a phone call.

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:42.640
You talk and the device talks back, instead of a walkie-talkie that only goes one way at

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.040
a time.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.140
Session management is the device keeping track of which chat you are in.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:51.980
It is like a group text that stays in its own thread so messages do not spill everywhere.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:56.620
However, handling interruptions means you can cut in while it is speaking, the way you

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:58.720
jump in when someone at the table is talking.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:01.140
Security features are being added too.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:06.080
If the face check fails three times, the system asks you to prove it is you with your iPhone.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:10.480
Keep getting locked out and the weight stretch, growing as long as eight hours.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:13.680
The face check is like unlocking your phone with your face.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:18.580
The growing weight is like a timeout that lasts longer each time someone keeps guessing wrong.

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:18.700
Long.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.680
Home view is scheduled to reach stores on November 13 in selected countries including

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:29.380
the United States, Britain, Canada, Australia, New Zealand, India, Singapore, and South

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:29.860
Africa.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.820
The starting price is $299 in the United States.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.600
The feature that would actually run third party chatbots is still described as not fully

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:39.100
wired up.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:43.440
Third party just means chatbots from other companies, not Apple's own.

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.120
No one can say exactly when or whether that part will appear.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:51.680
year. For families this could mean choosing the AI voice that explains homework clearly.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.300
It could also mean one that remembers the right smart light settings instead of being stuck

00:02:56.300 --> 00:03:00.960
with one company's style. It is like being allowed to pick which teacher to ask instead

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.300
of having only one person at the front of the class.

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:08.960
Students might ask one chat bot for step-by-step science help, while parents ask another for

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:13.840
quick calendar summaries. You cannot try home view yet. You can already compare how different

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:20.360
chatbots answer the same question. Open both chat GPT and clawed in your browser. Type explain

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:26.615
photosynthesis like I am 12, and watch how each one teaches the same idea. Your phone keyboard

00:03:26.615 --> 00:03:31.875
already guesses the next word while you type. That tiny trick is the whole engine behind these chat

00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:37.715
bots, stretched until it looks like a real conversation. First, the system studies huge collections of

00:03:37.715 --> 00:03:43.695
books, websites, and chats. It learns which words usually follow which other words. The way you learn

00:03:43.695 --> 00:03:48.695
song lyrics by hearing them over and over. Next you ask a question and it does not think

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:53.535
the way a person does. It just keeps picking the most likely next piece until a full answer

00:03:53.535 --> 00:03:58.915
sits there. Then each little chunk it reads or writes is called a token, roughly one word

00:03:58.915 --> 00:04:05.095
or part of a word. Picture tokens as Lego bricks. The model snaps one brick on, then the next

00:04:05.095 --> 00:04:10.775
until the sentence is a whole build. Last, the more tokens it can handle at once, the longer

00:04:10.775 --> 00:04:15.095
the conversation or document it can keep track of without dropping earlier details.

00:04:15.695 --> 00:04:17.235
Treat that limit like a backpack.

00:04:17.855 --> 00:04:20.695
Fill it with too many bricks and something old has to fall out.

00:04:21.215 --> 00:04:25.115
That is why a chatbot can suddenly lose the thread if your chat gets really long.

00:04:25.715 --> 00:04:28.215
The backpack is full, so the early stuff is gone.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:33.535
What you are talking to is an autocomplete engine that got so good at guessing it can write essays,

00:04:34.135 --> 00:04:36.815
answer science questions, or even help plan a project.

00:04:36.815 --> 00:04:42.491
The mystery is mostly speed and scale, not a brain hiding in the computer. Open

00:04:42.491 --> 00:04:48.831
AI co-founder Andre Carpathi used the AI chatbot clawed, the decoder reports, to sort

00:04:48.831 --> 00:04:53.951
a mountain of old comments. He ran through 43 million hacker news comments and turned them

00:04:53.951 --> 00:05:00.331
into a clean list of 6,454 recommended videos. Hacker news is a long-running site where

00:05:00.331 --> 00:05:05.771
people in tech share links and leave comments. 43 million comments is far more than anyone

00:05:05.771 --> 00:05:10.291
could read by hand in a weekend. He built a whole video site in that one weekend.

00:05:10.911 --> 00:05:15.331
The result is a handpicked feed that he says beats YouTube's own suggestions for finding

00:05:15.331 --> 00:05:20.751
interesting tech talks and tutorials. It is like having a super fast helper who can read a mountain

00:05:20.751 --> 00:05:26.111
of notes while you just describe what you want. One person with no coding team did it by chatting

00:05:26.111 --> 00:05:31.591
with an AI instead of writing code from scratch. You can try a tiny version of that same weekend

00:05:31.591 --> 00:05:37.911
project right now. Open Clawed or Chat GPT on your phone or laptop and paste a short list of

00:05:37.911 --> 00:05:43.551
video titles you like. Type group these into Beginner, Intermediate and Advanced Tech Talks

00:05:43.551 --> 00:05:49.031
and give each group a short reason why it fits. The AI will sort them and explain its choices.

00:05:50.106 --> 00:05:55.166
One shopper on Reddit takes a quick photo of the entire wine shelf and asks Chat GPT which

00:05:55.166 --> 00:06:00.386
bottle would go well with Curry, or whatever they are cooking. The Chatbot reads the labels,

00:06:00.386 --> 00:06:04.926
tables, prices, and grape types from the picture, and gives a recommendation, plus reasons

00:06:04.926 --> 00:06:06.026
why it might taste good.

00:06:06.606 --> 00:06:08.766
It works even when the photo is a little blurry.

00:06:09.326 --> 00:06:12.726
It often matches what a wine expert would pick, but much faster.

00:06:13.286 --> 00:06:17.766
It is like standing in the aisle with someone who can read every label at once, then tying

00:06:17.766 --> 00:06:19.466
those bottles to the meal in your cart.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:24.786
Next time you are at the store, open the chat GPT app on your phone and snap the shelf.

00:06:25.346 --> 00:06:29.786
Type which of these would taste good with pasta, and you might find a new favorite without

00:06:29.786 --> 00:06:35.026
guessing. The same trick works for any meal. Just add the dish you are planning and let the chat

00:06:35.026 --> 00:06:41.009
bot suggest based on the actual bottles in front of you. 50% of people in Spain who go online,

00:06:41.609 --> 00:06:47.209
telecom paper reports used an AI chat bot at least once during the second quarter of 2026.

00:06:47.909 --> 00:06:52.589
These tools are moving from something tech people try to something lots of regular people are testing

00:06:52.589 --> 00:06:58.189
out. That's it for today. Remember, every AI expert started exactly where you are right now.

00:06:58.189 --> 00:07:02.069
Now, if something we talked about today made you curious, go try it.

00:07:02.369 --> 00:07:03.989
That's literally how learning works.

00:07:04.509 --> 00:07:07.609
Stay curious, keep experimenting, and we'll see you tomorrow.

